'''''Mycolicibacter kumamotonensis''''' (formerly ''Mycobacterium kumamotonense'') is a species of bacteria.<ref name="Masaki"/><br />
[[Etymology]]: kumamotonensis, pertaining to [[Kumamoto Prefecture]] in [[Japan]], where the type strain was isolated.

==Description==
*Slowly growing, [[nonchromogenic]].

==Pathogenesis==
{{Empty section|date=July 2010}}

==Type strain==
*First isolated in [[Kumamoto Prefecture]], [[Japan]] from a clinical specimen.<ref name="Masaki"/>

